{"id":"game-09-exploration-system","group":"game","groupLabel":"Game Design","number":"09","title":"Exploration System","summary":"Defines exploration fantasy, regional identity, traversal, discoveries, points of interest, rewards and how world knowledge feeds progression.","sourceFile":"Game Design/09 - Exploration System.docx","meta":{"status":"DRAFT","version":"0.15.7","owner":"J. Crow","last_updated":"08/20/2026"},"headings":[{"level":1,"text":"1. Exploration Fantasy"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":2,"text":"Core fantasy"},{"level":1,"text":"Regional differentiation"},{"level":3,"text":"Visual identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Cultural identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Mechanical identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Economic identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Narrative identity"},{"level":1,"text":"Historical examples"},{"level":3,"text":"Arcane Kingdom"},{"level":3,"text":"Kingdom of the Archangels"},{"level":3,"text":"Ministry of Whispers"},{"level":1,"text":"2. Movement"},{"level":2,"text":"Basic movement"},{"level":1,"text":"Sprint"},{"level":3,"text":"Free sprinting"},{"level":1,"text":"Jumping"},{"level":1,"text":"Climbing"},{"level":3,"text":"Why?"},{"level":1,"text":"Special character mobility"},{"level":1,"text":"Teleportation"},{"level":3,"text":"Travel Point / Waypoint"},{"level":3,"text":"Rule"},{"level":1,"text":"Restrictions"},{"level":1,"text":"3. Points of Interest"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":2,"text":"Cities"},{"level":1,"text":"Towns and settlements"},{"level":1,"text":"Dungeons"},{"level":3,"text":"Story Dungeon"},{"level":3,"text":"Exploration Dungeon"},{"level":3,"text":"Progression Dungeon"},{"level":3,"text":"Weekly Dungeon"},{"level":1,"text":"Ruins"},{"level":1,"text":"Secrets"},{"level":1,"text":"NPCs"},{"level":3,"text":"Functional"},{"level":3,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":3,"text":"Dynamic"},{"level":1,"text":"World events"},{"level":1,"text":"Resources"},{"level":1,"text":"Bosses and minibosses"},{"level":1,"text":"Travel Points"},{"level":1,"text":"4. Discovery Rewards"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":1,"text":"Functional rewards"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative rewards"},{"level":1,"text":"Access rewards"},{"level":1,"text":"Cosmetic rewards"},{"level":1,"text":"How to avoid filling the map with markers"},{"level":3,"text":"Visible from the beginning"},{"level":3,"text":"Discovered by proximity"},{"level":3,"text":"Unmarked"},{"level":1,"text":"Rumor system"},{"level":1,"text":"Density rule"},{"level":1,"text":"5. Puzzles and Interactions"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":1,"text":"Puzzle types"},{"level":2,"text":"Elemental"},{"level":1,"text":"Environmental"},{"level":1,"text":"Logic-based"},{"level":1,"text":"Light-based"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":1,"text":"Professions"},{"level":1,"text":"How to avoid monotony"},{"level":3,"text":"Introduction"},{"level":3,"text":"Combination"},{"level":3,"text":"Variation"},{"level":1,"text":"6. World Danger"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":1,"text":"Safe zones"},{"level":1,"text":"Normal zones"},{"level":1,"text":"Hostile zones"},{"level":1,"text":"High-risk zones"},{"level":1,"text":"Recommended level"},{"level":3,"text":"Recommended Power"},{"level":1,"text":"Weather"},{"level":3,"text":"Rain"},{"level":3,"text":"Storm"},{"level":3,"text":"Snow"},{"level":3,"text":"Heat"},{"level":1,"text":"Environmental status effects"},{"level":1,"text":"Preparation"},{"level":1,"text":"Enemies"},{"level":1,"text":"Signposting"},{"level":1,"text":"7. Vertical Slice Scope"},{"level":2,"text":"Development"},{"level":1,"text":"Vertical Slice region"},{"level":3,"text":"1 representative micro-region"},{"level":1,"text":"Required movement"},{"level":3,"text":"Mandatory"},{"level":3,"text":"Optional if validated by the prototype"},{"level":1,"text":"Minimum Points of Interest"},{"level":3,"text":"5–8 meaningful POIs"},{"level":1,"text":"Puzzles"},{"level":3,"text":"1 basic puzzle"},{"level":3,"text":"1 combined puzzle"},{"level":1,"text":"Environmental storytelling"},{"level":1,"text":"Resources"},{"level":1,"text":"World Danger"},{"level":1,"text":"Systems outside the Vertical Slice"},{"level":1,"text":"What it must demonstrate"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"SYMPHONIA IUSTITIAE"},{"type":"title","text":"09 - Exploration System"},{"type":"p","text":"Movement, Discovery, and World Activities"},{"type":"table","table":0},{"type":"h1","text":"1. Exploration Fantasy"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"The exploration fantasy of Symphony of Justice should make the player feel that they are entering territories with their own history, culture, conflicts, and rules, rather than simply moving through maps built to connect one quest to another."},{"type":"p","text":"Exploration should primarily create four feelings:"},{"type":"p","text":"CURIOSITY → DISCOVERY → DANGER → UNDERSTANDING"},{"type":"p","text":"The current documentation already establishes that the protagonist initially enters many of the world's conflicts as an outsider, and that an important part of their experience involves learning about different cultures, organizations, and perspectives."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, the world should feel like something that existed before the player's arrival."},{"type":"h2","text":"Core fantasy"},{"type":"p","text":"The experience should convey: “I am entering a place with rules, secrets, and events that I do not yet understand.”"},{"type":"p","text":"We do not want the map to function only as a surface that the player clears of icons. Each region must contain enough visual, narrative, and gameplay clues for the player to learn about it simply by traveling through it."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"p","text":"architecture;"},{"type":"p","text":"climate;"},{"type":"p","text":"NPC behavior;"},{"type":"p","text":"enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"resources;"},{"type":"p","text":"music;"},{"type":"p","text":"ruins;"},{"type":"p","text":"documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"paths;"},{"type":"p","text":"dangers;"},{"type":"p","text":"objects;"},{"type":"p","text":"remnants of past events."},{"type":"h1","text":"Regional differentiation"},{"type":"p","text":"Each region must have at least five layers of identity:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Visual identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Architecture, vegetation, lighting, climate, and color."},{"type":"h3","text":"Cultural identity"},{"type":"p","text":"How its inhabitants live, what they believe, how they organize themselves, and what they consider just."},{"type":"h3","text":"Mechanical identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Which types of traversal, puzzles, enemies, or dangers appear most frequently."},{"type":"h3","text":"Economic identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Which materials, resources, and activities can be found there."},{"type":"h3","text":"Narrative identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Which events and conflicts are tied to that region."},{"type":"p","text":"The Game Vision already establishes that every region should contribute its own culture, architecture, history, characters, enemies, materials, quests, activities, secrets, Dungeons, bosses, and distinctive mechanics."},{"type":"h1","text":"Historical examples"},{"type":"p","text":"The original documentation already proposes specific differences."},{"type":"h3","text":"Arcane Kingdom"},{"type":"p","text":"Associated with:"},{"type":"p","text":"darkness;"},{"type":"p","text":"judgment;"},{"type":"p","text":"punishment;"},{"type":"p","text":"balance."},{"type":"p","text":"Its puzzles could use:"},{"type":"p","text":"decisions;"},{"type":"p","text":"scales;"},{"type":"p","text":"chains;"},{"type":"p","text":"judicial symbols;"},{"type":"p","text":"dark areas;"},{"type":"p","text":"tests of interpretation."},{"type":"h3","text":"Kingdom of the Archangels"},{"type":"p","text":"Related to:"},{"type":"p","text":"light;"},{"type":"p","text":"mercy;"},{"type":"p","text":"souls;"},{"type":"p","text":"spirituality."},{"type":"p","text":"It may use:"},{"type":"p","text":"mirrors;"},{"type":"p","text":"reflections;"},{"type":"p","text":"beams of light;"},{"type":"p","text":"lost souls;"},{"type":"p","text":"illusions;"},{"type":"p","text":"paths of light."},{"type":"h3","text":"Ministry of Whispers"},{"type":"p","text":"The documentation proposes an identity more closely tied to:"},{"type":"p","text":"mazes;"},{"type":"p","text":"patterns;"},{"type":"p","text":"order;"},{"type":"p","text":"recognition."},{"type":"p","text":"This can turn exploration into a challenge of:"},{"type":"p","text":"orientation;"},{"type":"p","text":"memory;"},{"type":"p","text":"patterns;"},{"type":"p","text":"internal routes;"},{"type":"p","text":"investigation."},{"type":"p","text":"These differences already appear conceptually in the historical document."},{"type":"h1","text":"2. Movement"},{"type":"p","text":"We must be especially clear here: the historical documentation does not define a complete movement system."},{"type":"p","text":"Under the approaches considered so far, the main way to move through this world is by following exploration paths: the player walks toward a destination to discover what is there. The player may also glide, climb, and swim, but travel from one major point to another is normally handled through a lore element called the “Shinigami Trains.”"},{"type":"p","text":"According to the game's story, the gods of death are also responsible for transporting people, usually by rail, although carriages or teleportation points in specific areas may also be used."},{"type":"h2","text":"Basic movement"},{"type":"p","text":"The player directly controls a character in a real-time 3D environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Basic movement must include:"},{"type":"p","text":"walking;"},{"type":"p","text":"running;"},{"type":"p","text":"sprinting;"},{"type":"p","text":"jumping;"},{"type":"p","text":"falling;"},{"type":"p","text":"dodging;"},{"type":"p","text":"contextual interaction."},{"type":"p","text":"It must feel responsive because exploration and combat occur within one continuous experience."},{"type":"h1","text":"Sprint"},{"type":"p","text":"Sprint should allow fast movement without turning traversal into a waiting period. I initially propose:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Free sprinting"},{"type":"p","text":"No permanent stamina drain during normal travel. Stamina may be reserved for special actions if it becomes necessary later."},{"type":"p","text":"I do not recommend making several minutes of running continuously consume a resource, because that creates friction without producing an interesting decision."},{"type":"h1","text":"Jumping"},{"type":"p","text":"It should allow the player to:"},{"type":"p","text":"overcome obstacles;"},{"type":"p","text":"reach small platforms;"},{"type":"p","text":"initiate selected interactions;"},{"type":"p","text":"complement the character's mobility."},{"type":"p","text":"It does not need to become extremely precise platforming."},{"type":"h1","text":"Climbing"},{"type":"p","text":"I propose limited climbing rather than universal climbing on every surface."},{"type":"p","text":"It may use:"},{"type":"p","text":"ledges;"},{"type":"p","text":"marked walls;"},{"type":"p","text":"structures;"},{"type":"p","text":"roots;"},{"type":"p","text":"ruins;"},{"type":"p","text":"handholds."},{"type":"h3","text":"Why?"},{"type":"p","text":"It provides better control over:"},{"type":"p","text":"level design;"},{"type":"p","text":"routes;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"optimization;"},{"type":"p","text":"performance;"},{"type":"p","text":"visual readability."},{"type":"p","text":"Completely free climbing would multiply design costs and make it easier to break routes or puzzles."},{"type":"h1","text":"Special character mobility"},{"type":"p","text":"Certain characters may have unique utilities:"},{"type":"p","text":"extended jump;"},{"type":"p","text":"gliding;"},{"type":"p","text":"dash;"},{"type":"p","text":"vertical mobility;"},{"type":"p","text":"aquatic movement;"},{"type":"p","text":"platform creation;"},{"type":"p","text":"short-range teleportation."},{"type":"p","text":"However, we must preserve the rule already established in the Game Vision and Gacha System: no mandatory content may require ownership of a specific Gacha character."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, a special ability may: accelerate or facilitate"},{"type":"p","text":"but it must not: provide exclusive access to essential content."},{"type":"h1","text":"Teleportation"},{"type":"p","text":"I do recommend including a Fast Travel system."},{"type":"p","text":"Once an important location has been discovered, it may become a:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Travel Point / Waypoint"},{"type":"p","text":"It may exist in:"},{"type":"p","text":"cities;"},{"type":"p","text":"camps;"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon entrances;"},{"type":"p","text":"shrines;"},{"type":"p","text":"lore-specific structures."},{"type":"p","text":"The player must physically reach the point at least once to activate it."},{"type":"h3","text":"Rule"},{"type":"p","text":"First, the location is discovered on foot; afterward, fast travel is allowed."},{"type":"h1","text":"Restrictions"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not allow Fast Travel during:"},{"type":"p","text":"combat;"},{"type":"p","text":"chases;"},{"type":"p","text":"narrative encounters;"},{"type":"p","text":"special zones;"},{"type":"p","text":"selected Dungeons."},{"type":"h1","text":"3. Points of Interest"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Points of Interest are locations that can break up the routine of traversal and give the player a reason to stop."},{"type":"p","text":"The player should be able to see something in the distance and think: “I want to know what is there.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Not every POI should appear on the map immediately."},{"type":"h2","text":"Cities"},{"type":"p","text":"They function as hubs for:"},{"type":"p","text":"narrative;"},{"type":"p","text":"commerce;"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"crafting;"},{"type":"p","text":"quests;"},{"type":"p","text":"services;"},{"type":"p","text":"culture."},{"type":"p","text":"Each city must visually represent the society of its region. We do not want interchangeable cities."},{"type":"h1","text":"Towns and settlements"},{"type":"p","text":"Smaller in scale than a capital, they may offer:"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"shops;"},{"type":"p","text":"small stories;"},{"type":"p","text":"hunts;"},{"type":"p","text":"resources;"},{"type":"p","text":"professions."},{"type":"h1","text":"Dungeons"},{"type":"p","text":"The historical documentation defines Dungeons as progressive experiences capable of telling stories and increasing in difficulty, including maze formats and elemental or national themes. They may be divided into:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Story Dungeon"},{"type":"p","text":"Narrative."},{"type":"h3","text":"Exploration Dungeon"},{"type":"p","text":"Puzzles + traversal."},{"type":"h3","text":"Progression Dungeon"},{"type":"p","text":"Resources."},{"type":"h3","text":"Weekly Dungeon"},{"type":"p","text":"Recurring content."},{"type":"h1","text":"Ruins"},{"type":"p","text":"They are especially important for environmental storytelling."},{"type":"p","text":"They may contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"relics;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"Codex entries;"},{"type":"p","text":"historical remains."},{"type":"p","text":"This connects directly with the original exploration quests, whose goal is to uncover the world's past and origins."},{"type":"h1","text":"Secrets"},{"type":"p","text":"They may appear as:"},{"type":"p","text":"hidden rooms;"},{"type":"p","text":"secondary routes;"},{"type":"p","text":"caves;"},{"type":"p","text":"documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"chests;"},{"type":"p","text":"rare encounters;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"narrative references."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal secret should not rely solely on being hidden behind an invisible wall; there should be some kind of clue. In addition, it must not be obtainable only by owning a specific character. The protagonist must be capable of obtaining it. For example, if it requires navigating a maze or using an element, the Traveler must be able to complete it. A different character may make discovery easier or faster, but must not be required."},{"type":"h1","text":"NPCs"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs may have three functions:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Functional"},{"type":"p","text":"Commerce, crafting, and services."},{"type":"h3","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"Stories and context."},{"type":"h3","text":"Dynamic"},{"type":"p","text":"Activities, emergencies, events, or encounters."},{"type":"p","text":"World exploration should allow the player to meet inhabitants even outside main quests."},{"type":"h1","text":"World events"},{"type":"p","text":"Situations that occur while traveling:"},{"type":"p","text":"enemies attacking;"},{"type":"p","text":"an NPC asking for help;"},{"type":"p","text":"a convoy;"},{"type":"p","text":"a special creature;"},{"type":"p","text":"an elemental phenomenon;"},{"type":"p","text":"a regional event."},{"type":"p","text":"They may appear temporarily and break the predictability of traversal."},{"type":"h1","text":"Resources"},{"type":"p","text":"They include:"},{"type":"p","text":"plants;"},{"type":"p","text":"minerals;"},{"type":"p","text":"creatures;"},{"type":"p","text":"ingredients;"},{"type":"p","text":"regional materials;"},{"type":"p","text":"crafting materials;"},{"type":"p","text":"ascension materials."},{"type":"p","text":"This connects directly with the Alchemy, Cooking, and Blacksmithing systems that the original documentation presents as complementary activities."},{"type":"h1","text":"Bosses and minibosses"},{"type":"p","text":"The documents already contain lists of:"},{"type":"p","text":"exploration enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"minibosses;"},{"type":"p","text":"Evolution Bosses;"},{"type":"p","text":"Weekly Bosses."},{"type":"p","text":"Some may function as permanent POIs."},{"type":"p","text":"Others may function as roaming encounters."},{"type":"h1","text":"Travel Points"},{"type":"p","text":"They serve as:"},{"type":"p","text":"Fast Travel points;"},{"type":"p","text":"checkpoints;"},{"type":"p","text":"orientation aids;"},{"type":"p","text":"cultural landmarks."},{"type":"p","text":"They must be integrated into the lore and should not look like antennas placed there only because the UI requires them."},{"type":"h1","text":"4. Discovery Rewards"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Exploration must produce at least one of four rewards:"},{"type":"p","text":"POWER + KNOWLEDGE + ACCESS + EXPRESSION"},{"type":"h1","text":"Functional rewards"},{"type":"p","text":"materials;"},{"type":"p","text":"currency;"},{"type":"p","text":"items;"},{"type":"p","text":"experience;"},{"type":"p","text":"recipes;"},{"type":"p","text":"equipment;"},{"type":"p","text":"regional resources."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative rewards"},{"type":"p","text":"Codex entries;"},{"type":"p","text":"documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"conversations;"},{"type":"p","text":"journals;"},{"type":"p","text":"archives;"},{"type":"p","text":"secrets;"},{"type":"p","text":"memories;"},{"type":"p","text":"historical information."},{"type":"p","text":"The Game Vision already establishes that the progressive discovery of information must form part of the reward for advancing."},{"type":"h1","text":"Access rewards"},{"type":"p","text":"Exploration may unlock:"},{"type":"p","text":"Waypoints;"},{"type":"p","text":"routes;"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeons;"},{"type":"p","text":"hidden entrances;"},{"type":"p","text":"quests;"},{"type":"p","text":"bosses;"},{"type":"p","text":"activities."},{"type":"h1","text":"Cosmetic rewards"},{"type":"p","text":"recipes;"},{"type":"p","text":"designs;"},{"type":"p","text":"decorations;"},{"type":"p","text":"titles;"},{"type":"p","text":"profile elements;"},{"type":"p","text":"special collectibles."},{"type":"h1","text":"How to avoid filling the map with markers"},{"type":"p","text":"The map should not automatically display everything."},{"type":"p","text":"I propose three levels:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Visible from the beginning"},{"type":"p","text":"major cities;"},{"type":"p","text":"known narrative objectives;"},{"type":"p","text":"important Travel Points."},{"type":"h3","text":"Discovered by proximity"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeons;"},{"type":"p","text":"activities;"},{"type":"p","text":"settlements;"},{"type":"p","text":"bosses."},{"type":"h3","text":"Unmarked"},{"type":"p","text":"secrets;"},{"type":"p","text":"small puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"chests;"},{"type":"p","text":"hidden events;"},{"type":"p","text":"documents."},{"type":"h1","text":"Rumor system"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs, discovered maps, or documents may add approximate markers."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"“There is an abandoned structure north of the forest.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of:"},{"type":"p","text":"CHEST EXACTLY 126 METERS AWAY."},{"type":"p","text":"This preserves discovery."},{"type":"h1","text":"Density rule"},{"type":"p","text":"We do not need to reward the player every twenty meters."},{"type":"p","text":"An enjoyable map alternates between:"},{"type":"p","text":"space → anticipation → discovery → reward."},{"type":"p","text":"If everything has an icon, nothing feels special."},{"type":"h1","text":"5. Puzzles and Interactions"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Puzzles must use the identity of each region and the elemental systems."},{"type":"p","text":"They should not feel like arbitrary minigames attached to the world."},{"type":"h1","text":"Puzzle types"},{"type":"h2","text":"Elemental"},{"type":"p","text":"They use:"},{"type":"p","text":"Water;"},{"type":"p","text":"Fire;"},{"type":"p","text":"Ice;"},{"type":"p","text":"Electro;"},{"type":"p","text":"Plant;"},{"type":"p","text":"Wind;"},{"type":"p","text":"Earth;"},{"type":"p","text":"Pure Powers."},{"type":"p","text":"The elemental matrix we have already defined creates interesting possibilities because some reactions literally modify the terrain through:"},{"type":"p","text":"Swamp;"},{"type":"p","text":"Barriers;"},{"type":"p","text":"Magma;"},{"type":"p","text":"Germination;"},{"type":"p","text":"Electric Zone;"},{"type":"p","text":"Quicksand."},{"type":"p","text":"This allows combat and exploration to connect."},{"type":"h1","text":"Environmental"},{"type":"p","text":"moving structures;"},{"type":"p","text":"finding routes;"},{"type":"p","text":"opening doors;"},{"type":"p","text":"activating mechanisms;"},{"type":"p","text":"manipulating heights;"},{"type":"p","text":"using water or wind currents."},{"type":"h1","text":"Logic-based"},{"type":"p","text":"Especially appropriate for regions such as the Arcane Kingdom or the Ministry:"},{"type":"p","text":"patterns;"},{"type":"p","text":"sequences;"},{"type":"p","text":"judgment;"},{"type":"p","text":"balance;"},{"type":"p","text":"symbols."},{"type":"h1","text":"Light-based"},{"type":"p","text":"Appropriate for the Archangels:"},{"type":"p","text":"mirrors;"},{"type":"p","text":"prisms;"},{"type":"p","text":"beams;"},{"type":"p","text":"reflections."},{"type":"p","text":"This type of proposal already appears in the historical documentation."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"The player uses information found in:"},{"type":"p","text":"documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"statues;"},{"type":"p","text":"dialogue;"},{"type":"p","text":"symbols."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"A record explains an ancient order of judgment. The player later uses that knowledge to open a chamber. In this way: knowing the lore = having a gameplay tool."},{"type":"h1","text":"Professions"},{"type":"p","text":"Certain professions may facilitate interactions."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Blacksmith quickly repairs a mechanism."},{"type":"p","text":"Medic identifies a poisonous plant."},{"type":"p","text":"Explorer detects clues."},{"type":"p","text":"Alchemist identifies a substance."},{"type":"p","text":"But once again:"},{"type":"p","text":"facilitate ≠ block."},{"type":"p","text":"There must always be a basic solution accessible to the player."},{"type":"h1","text":"How to avoid monotony"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not repeat:"},{"type":"p","text":"“light five totems”"},{"type":"p","text":"twenty times."},{"type":"p","text":"Each puzzle family may evolve through three levels."},{"type":"h3","text":"Introduction"},{"type":"p","text":"Teaches the rule."},{"type":"h3","text":"Combination"},{"type":"p","text":"Combines two rules."},{"type":"h3","text":"Variation"},{"type":"p","text":"Introduces pressure, time, enemies, or inversion."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Light 1: orient one mirror."},{"type":"p","text":"Light 2: orient three mirrors."},{"type":"p","text":"Light 3: orient mirrors while a light source changes position."},{"type":"h1","text":"6. World Danger"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"The world should not feel completely safe outside selected combat encounters."},{"type":"p","text":"There must be a clear distinction among:"},{"type":"p","text":"civilization → frontier → hostile territory → extreme zone."},{"type":"h1","text":"Safe zones"},{"type":"p","text":"cities;"},{"type":"p","text":"settlements;"},{"type":"p","text":"selected camps."},{"type":"p","text":"They do not contain normal combat."},{"type":"h1","text":"Normal zones"},{"type":"p","text":"They contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"common enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"resources;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"encounters."},{"type":"p","text":"They represent standard exploration."},{"type":"h1","text":"Hostile zones"},{"type":"p","text":"They may include:"},{"type":"p","text":"stronger enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"environmental hazards;"},{"type":"p","text":"higher density;"},{"type":"p","text":"fewer safe points;"},{"type":"p","text":"better rewards."},{"type":"h1","text":"High-risk zones"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced content."},{"type":"p","text":"They may contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"elite enemies;"},{"type":"p","text":"minibosses;"},{"type":"p","text":"extreme weather;"},{"type":"p","text":"status effects;"},{"type":"p","text":"complex puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"rare resources."},{"type":"h1","text":"Recommended level"},{"type":"p","text":"I do not recommend using a rigid wall such as:"},{"type":"p","text":"“You cannot enter until level 40.”"},{"type":"p","text":"It is preferable to use:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Recommended Power"},{"type":"p","text":"The player may enter earlier at their own risk."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Recommended Team Level: 45"},{"type":"p","text":"This allows for:"},{"type":"p","text":"skilled players;"},{"type":"p","text":"early exploration;"},{"type":"p","text":"curiosity;"},{"type":"p","text":"self-imposed challenges."},{"type":"h1","text":"Weather"},{"type":"p","text":"It may have gameplay consequences."},{"type":"h3","text":"Rain"},{"type":"p","text":"wet surfaces;"},{"type":"p","text":"greater conductivity;"},{"type":"p","text":"reduced presence of fire."},{"type":"h3","text":"Storm"},{"type":"p","text":"Electro;"},{"type":"p","text":"visibility;"},{"type":"p","text":"hazards."},{"type":"h3","text":"Snow"},{"type":"p","text":"mobility;"},{"type":"p","text":"Cryo;"},{"type":"p","text":"freezing."},{"type":"h3","text":"Heat"},{"type":"p","text":"resource consumption;"},{"type":"p","text":"fire;"},{"type":"p","text":"exhaustion."},{"type":"p","text":"However, not every region needs a survival system."},{"type":"h1","text":"Environmental status effects"},{"type":"p","text":"They may include:"},{"type":"p","text":"cold;"},{"type":"p","text":"heat;"},{"type":"p","text":"corruption;"},{"type":"p","text":"Chaos;"},{"type":"p","text":"toxicity;"},{"type":"p","text":"darkness;"},{"type":"p","text":"curse."},{"type":"p","text":"These should create understandable pressure while avoiding: rapid death because the player forgot to equip an item in a menu."},{"type":"h1","text":"Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"The Cooking and Alchemy systems can help the player prepare for expeditions."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"p","text":"food that protects against cold;"},{"type":"p","text":"elemental resistance;"},{"type":"p","text":"antidotes;"},{"type":"p","text":"temporary buffs."},{"type":"p","text":"This connects exploration with the economy and professions."},{"type":"h1","text":"Enemies"},{"type":"p","text":"The documents already distinguish exploration enemies from minibosses and include a wide variety of creatures."},{"type":"p","text":"They should not appear randomly in every region."},{"type":"p","text":"Their presence must make ecological or narrative sense."},{"type":"h1","text":"Signposting"},{"type":"p","text":"Before the player enters a dangerous zone, the environment should communicate the danger through:"},{"type":"p","text":"music;"},{"type":"p","text":"corpses;"},{"type":"p","text":"architecture;"},{"type":"p","text":"weather;"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"VFX;"},{"type":"p","text":"visible enemies."},{"type":"h1","text":"7. Vertical Slice Scope"},{"type":"h2","text":"Development"},{"type":"p","text":"The Vertical Slice does not need to demonstrate a complete open world. The Game Vision already establishes that the initial prototype does not require an open world or multiple regions, and that the Vertical Slice should represent a small experience that is nevertheless considerably closer to final quality."},{"type":"p","text":"For exploration, we must demonstrate depth within a small space."},{"type":"h1","text":"Vertical Slice region"},{"type":"p","text":"I propose:"},{"type":"h3","text":"1 representative micro-region"},{"type":"p","text":"Not an entire nation."},{"type":"p","text":"It must contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"a small settlement or safe point;"},{"type":"p","text":"a main route;"},{"type":"p","text":"at least one secondary route;"},{"type":"p","text":"a hostile zone;"},{"type":"p","text":"a ruin or structure;"},{"type":"p","text":"a small Dungeon or interior space;"},{"type":"p","text":"a Boss area or major encounter."},{"type":"h1","text":"Required movement"},{"type":"h3","text":"Mandatory"},{"type":"p","text":"walking;"},{"type":"p","text":"running;"},{"type":"p","text":"sprinting;"},{"type":"p","text":"jumping;"},{"type":"p","text":"dodging;"},{"type":"p","text":"interaction;"},{"type":"p","text":"minimal Fast Travel."},{"type":"h3","text":"Optional if validated by the prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"limited climbing;"},{"type":"p","text":"contextual mobility."},{"type":"h1","text":"Minimum Points of Interest"},{"type":"p","text":"The demo should contain approximately:"},{"type":"h3","text":"5–8 meaningful POIs"},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"p","text":"settlement;"},{"type":"p","text":"Travel Point;"},{"type":"p","text":"ruin;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzle;"},{"type":"p","text":"enemy encounter;"},{"type":"p","text":"special resource;"},{"type":"p","text":"secret;"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon/Boss."},{"type":"p","text":"We do not need forty icons. We need each one to demonstrate a different type of interaction."},{"type":"h1","text":"Puzzles"},{"type":"p","text":"The Vertical Slice should show:"},{"type":"h3","text":"1 basic puzzle"},{"type":"p","text":"Teaches one rule."},{"type":"h3","text":"1 combined puzzle"},{"type":"p","text":"Uses that rule together with an element, the environment, or combat."},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates that exploration and gameplay form a single system."},{"type":"h1","text":"Environmental storytelling"},{"type":"p","text":"There must be at least:"},{"type":"p","text":"one document;"},{"type":"p","text":"one visual scene;"},{"type":"p","text":"one NPC;"},{"type":"p","text":"one piece of environmental evidence."},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is for a player to understand something about the location without receiving a long cinematic."},{"type":"h1","text":"Resources"},{"type":"p","text":"The player must be able to collect:"},{"type":"p","text":"a regional material;"},{"type":"p","text":"a crafting material;"},{"type":"p","text":"a narrative or special reward."},{"type":"p","text":"The player must then use at least one of them."},{"type":"p","text":"Example: gather an ingredient → craft a consumable → use it before the Boss."},{"type":"p","text":"This closes a small loop."},{"type":"h1","text":"World Danger"},{"type":"p","text":"The demo must contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"a safe zone;"},{"type":"p","text":"a normal zone;"},{"type":"p","text":"one clearly more dangerous zone."},{"type":"p","text":"We do not need a complete global weather system."},{"type":"p","text":"We can include a single representative environmental hazard."},{"type":"h1","text":"Systems outside the Vertical Slice"},{"type":"p","text":"I would not develop the following yet:"},{"type":"p","text":"the complete world;"},{"type":"p","text":"multiple nations;"},{"type":"p","text":"dynamic global weather;"},{"type":"p","text":"a seasonal cycle;"},{"type":"p","text":"a complete ecosystem;"},{"type":"p","text":"dozens of puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"housing;"},{"type":"p","text":"navigation;"},{"type":"p","text":"a complete Social Hub;"},{"type":"p","text":"persistent multiplayer;"},{"type":"p","text":"hundreds of NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"complex procedural world events;"},{"type":"p","text":"large-scale simulation systems."},{"type":"h1","text":"What it must demonstrate"},{"type":"p","text":"The question for the Vertical Slice will be: Does exploring this small place make me want to see what lies beyond it?"},{"type":"p","text":"At the end, a player should be able to say:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I understand how to move”;"},{"type":"p","text":"“I found something because I was curious”;"},{"type":"p","text":"“the location had an identity”;"},{"type":"p","text":"“my exploration produced resources”;"},{"type":"p","text":"“I discovered something about the story”;"},{"type":"p","text":"“I found at least one thing that was not directly pointed out to me.”"},{"type":"p","text":"This connects with the current Experience Goals, in which one of the main metrics is precisely whether the player wants to continue exploring the world."}],"tables":[[["Status","DRAFT","Version","0.15.7"],["Owner","J. Crow","Last updated","08/20/2026"]]]}